    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61284" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωμ-αστής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>reveller</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				212c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				5.4.7
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>member of a</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶμος, Πολέμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.46
				</span></i>
			 (Attica, <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>); title of play by Epicharmus.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> epith. of Dionysus,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				606
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in
			Egypt, <i>one who carries sacred images in procession</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. θεῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					519
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1265.9
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>.</div>
